47:## Main Business Entities And Tables\n.ai-factory/DESCRIPTION.md:149:### Products\n.ai-factory/DESCRIPTION.md:166:### Import / Update / Delete Tracking\n.ai-factory/DESCRIPTION.md:181:### Shop Binding And Remote IDs\n.ai-factory/DESCRIPTION.md:190:### Catalog Taxonomy And Shop Scope\n.ai-factory/DESCRIPTION.md:212:### Shops And Languages\n.ai-factory/DESCRIPTION.md:221:### SEO And AI\n.ai-factory/DESCRIPTION.md:228:### Backups\n.ai-factory/DESCRIPTION.md:232:## Key Relationships\n.ai-factory/DESCRIPTION.md:252:## Where To Look First When Debugging\n.ai-factory/DESCRIPTION.md:326:## Important Recent Regression History\n.ai-factory/DESCRIPTION.md:334:## Architecture\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:1:# Architecture: Modular Monolith\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:3:## Overview\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:4:Strateg Export Products should be maintained as a modular monolith on Laravel 13. The application is deployed as one codebase and one database, but its business behavior is already split into strong modules: imports, bindings, exports, updates, deletes, restores, translations, SEO synchronization, and external shop integrations.\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:8:## Decision Rationale\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:10:- **Tech stack:** PHP 8.5, Laravel 13, Filament 5, Livewire 4, PostgreSQL 18.\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:13:## Folder Structure\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:53:## Module Map\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:55:### Supports Layer\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:74:#### Support Service Groups\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:85:### Presentation Module\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:95:### Import Module\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:107:### Binding Module\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:120:### Export Module\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:130:### Remote API Boundary\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:148:### Update / Delete / Restore Modules\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:162:### Translation And SEO Module\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:174:## Dependency Rules\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:187:## Layer/Module Communication\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:207:## Data And Table Rules\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:218:## Investigation Guide\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:220:### If import is broken\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:232:### If binding is broken\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:249:### If export/update/delete is broken\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:263:### If restore is broken\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:276:### If translations or SEO are broken\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:291:## Key Principles\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:301:## Code Examples\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:303:### Filament Action Should Delegate To Workflow Code\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:324:### Binding Rules Must Stay Inside The Binding Service\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:349:## Anti-Patterns\n.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md:362:## Patch Awareness\nREADME.md:1:# Strateg Export Products\nREADME.md:5:The project imports products from Excel, Google Sheets, and the administration panel, normalizes the catalog in PostgreSQL, links products to stores, and performs export, update, deletion, and restoration through store APIs.\nREADME.md:7:## Quick Start\nREADME.md:14:## Example workflow\nREADME.md:20:## Features\nREADME.md:29:## Main Commands\nREADME.md:35:## Documentation\nREADME.md:58:## License\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:1:[← Product Import](product-import-batch-resource.md) · [Back to README](../README.md) · [Product Deletes →](product-delete-batch-resource.md)\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:3:# ProductUpdateBatchResource\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:5:## Purpose\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:9:## Resource Pages\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:17:## How to Use\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:26:## Statuses\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:34:## Main Actions\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:40:## Common Skip Reasons\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:48:## See Also\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:3:# Agent Collaboration\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:11:## Subagent orchestration policy\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:17:### Hard limits\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:55:### Nested delegation\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:84:### Before spawning\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:97:### Token and cost discipline\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:112:### Lifecycle\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:125:### Default strategy\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:143:## Roles and authority\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:174:- collect evidence from PostgreSQL and configured services while respecting project scope and read/write authorization;\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:204:## Delegation protocol\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:237:- PostgreSQL project index\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:257:## Concurrent work and write scopes\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:291:## Shared data and services\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:293:### AI Code Intelligence database\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:320:### Database write authorization\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:344:### Embeddings and paid operations\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:364:### Runtime services\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:383:## Browser and UI ownership\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:417:## Git handoff\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:446:## Required completion report\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:450:### Status\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:460:### Summary\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:464:### Evidence\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:481:### Files\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:493:### Verification\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:506:### Side effects\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:522:### Git\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:530:### Open items\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:546:## Primary-agent integration rules\ndocs/agent-collaboration.md:565:## See Also\ndocs/category-resource.md:1:[← Remote API Integration](remote-api-integration.md) · [Back to README](../README.md) · [Attributes →](attribute-resource.md)\ndocs/category-resource.md:3:# CategoryResource (Catalog → Categories)\ndocs/category-resource.md:5:## Purpose\ndocs/category-resource.md:9:## Resource Pages\ndocs/category-resource.md:17:## How to Use\ndocs/category-resource.md:21:## Filters and Statuses\ndocs/category-resource.md:25:## Main Actions\ndocs/category-resource.md:31:## Deletion\ndocs/category-resource.md:35:## See Also\ndocs/product-delete-batch-resource.md:1:[← Product Updates](product-update-batch-resource.md) · [Back to README](../README.md) · [Product Catalog →](product-resource.md)\ndocs/product-delete-batch-resource.md:3:# ProductDeleteResource\ndocs/product-delete-batch-resource.md:5:## Purpose\ndocs/product-delete-batch-resource.md:11:## Input modes\ndocs/product-delete-batch-resource.md:22:## Queue and execution\ndocs/product-delete-batch-resource.md:32:## Statuses\ndocs/product-delete-batch-resource.md:36:## See Also\ndocs/product-resource.md:1:[← Product Deletes](product-delete-batch-resource.md) · [Back to README](../README.md) · [Remote API Integration →](remote-api-integration.md)\ndocs/product-resource.md:3:# ProductResource (Catalog → Products)\ndocs/product-resource.md:5:## Purpose\ndocs/product-resource.md:9:## Resource Pages\ndocs/product-resource.md:17:## How to Use\ndocs/product-resource.md:21:## API Update Settings\ndocs/product-resource.md:25:## List Columns and Indicators\ndocs/product-resource.md:32:## See Also\ndocs/configuration.md:1:[← Architecture](architecture.md) · [Back to README](../README.md) · [Helper Functions →](helpers.md)\ndocs/configuration.md:3:# Configuration\ndocs/configuration.md:5:## Environment Files\ndocs/configuration.md:7:Development Docker configuration is stored in .docker/dev/env/. The .docker/dev/docker-compose.yml file loads shared and PostgreSQL variables into containers.\ndocs/configuration.md:9:The Laravel application is located in app-code/app. Its standard Laravel settings (.env and config/*.php) are applied inside PHP-FPM.\ndocs/configuration.md:13:## Stores\ndocs/configuration.md:31:## Languages\ndocs/configuration.md:35:## Queues and Background Tasks\ndocs/configuration.md:39:## See Also\ndocs/helpers.md:1:[← Configuration](configuration.md) · [Back to README](../README.md) · [Supports Reference →](supports.md)\ndocs/helpers.md:3:# Helper Functions\ndocs/helpers.md:5:The file app-code/app/app/Supports/helpers.php is loaded through autoload.files in composer.json. These functions are available throughout the Laravel application after the Composer autoloader is loaded.\ndocs/helpers.md:7:## Phones and Strings\ndocs/helpers.md:21:## HTML and URLs\ndocs/helpers.md:31:## Values and Arrays\ndocs/helpers.md:45:## Telegram\ndocs/helpers.md:55:## Dates, JSON, and Locales\ndocs/helpers.md:67:## Example\ndocs/helpers.md:73:## See Also\ndocs/attribute-resource.md:1:[← Categories](category-resource.md) · [Back to README](../README.md) · [Stores →](shop-resource.md)\ndocs/attribute-resource.md:3:# AttributeResource (Catalog → Attributes)\ndocs/attribute-resource.md:5:## Purpose\ndocs/attribute-resource.md:9:## Resource Pages\ndocs/attribute-resource.md:17:## How to Use\ndocs/attribute-resource.md:21:## Filters and Statuses\ndocs/attribute-resource.md:25:## Notifications\ndocs/attribute-resource.md:29:## See Also\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:1:[← Agent Collaboration](agent-collaboration.md) · [Back to README](../README.md)\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:3:# AI Code Intelligence\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:5:This project is indexed in the shared [AI Code Intelligence repository](../../../hobby/ai-code-intelligence). Its PostgreSQL database stores project-scoped source metadata, searchable chunks, and embeddings. Use it to discover likely files and concepts; verify every conclusion against this repository's source and, where relevant, tests or runtime behavior.\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:7:## Project identity and shared documentation\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:18:## Pick a tool for the question\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:26:| Unfamiliar business concept or design rationale  | PostgreSQL full-text plus vector search                         |\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:33:## Host tools and invocation\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:35:PostgreSQL and Node.js for the intelligence database run in Docker. Serena, `ast-grep`, and Tree-sitter Python bindings are host-side tools; a missing executable inside a container says nothing about host availability. Check the host before use:\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:57:## Search the shared index\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:59:The shared Compose file is `/home/kamaz/www/hobby/ai-code-intelligence/.docker/dev/docker-compose.yml`; the PostgreSQL service is `ai-code-intelligence-postgres-postgresql`. Resolve the current project ID by its slug in each session—never copy an ID from another project or search across tenants:\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:79:## What is indexed and what it can tell you\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:100:Chunks provide full-text and vector retrieval; symbol records help locate declarations. Source chunks use non-overlapping 80-line windows. Tree-sitter parsed the PHP sources without reported parse failures and extracted declaration symbols; stored symbol ranges use declaration lines, not full AST extents. `aic_symbol_relations` is empty, so the index cannot establish call or dependency paths. PostgreSQL FTS reports that words longer than 2,047 characters are ignored. Treat search results as leads and verify behavior in source and tests.\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:104:## Refreshing the index and paid embeddings\ndocs/ai-code-intelligence.md:112:## See Also\ndocs/architecture.md:1:[← Getting Started](getting-started.md) · [Back to README](../README.md) · [Configuration →](configuration.md)\ndocs/architecture.md:3:# Architecture\ndocs/architecture.md:5:## Overview\ndocs/architecture.md:7:The application is a Laravel modular monolith. Filament provides the administration interface, queued jobs process long-running operations, and services contain catalog rules and external-store integrations.\ndocs/architecture.md:15:    Local PostgreSQL + external store API\ndocs/architecture.md:17:## Main Directories\ndocs/architecture.md:27:| database/migrations | PostgreSQL schema                                    |\ndocs/architecture.md:30:## Catalog Flows\ndocs/architecture.md:40:## Module Boundaries\ndocs/architecture.md:50:## Supports Layer\ndocs/architecture.md:64:## See Also\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:1:[← Supports Reference](supports.md) · [Back to README](../README.md) · [Product Import →](product-import-batch-resource.md)\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:3:# Product Data Workflows\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:7:## Workflow overview\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:32:## Import and create products\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:46:## Export products to a shop\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:59:## Update products\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:75:## Delete products from a shop\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:81:## Restore products\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:92:## Status and audit behavior\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:103:## See Also\ndocs/getting-started.md:3:# Getting Started\ndocs/getting-started.md:5:## Requirements\ndocs/getting-started.md:11:The application runs in Docker containers with PHP 8.5, Laravel 12, Filament 5, Livewire 4, and PostgreSQL 18.\ndocs/getting-started.md:13:## Start the Development Environment\ndocs/getting-started.md:20:build-dev builds local images. up-dev starts PHP-FPM, Nginx, PostgreSQL, Redis, and cron. If images already exist, run only make up-dev.\ndocs/getting-started.md:22:## Check the Status\ndocs/getting-started.md:26:PHP-FPM and Nginx should be Up; PostgreSQL and Redis should pass their health checks.\ndocs/getting-started.md:28:## Application Commands\ndocs/getting-started.md:36:## Stop the Environment\ndocs/getting-started.md:40:## Next Steps\ndocs/getting-started.md:44:## See Also\ndocs/shop-resource.md:1:[← Attributes](attribute-resource.md) · [Back to README](../README.md) · [Store Languages →](shop-language-resource.