{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T07:52:14.708Z","ordinal":10636,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a0a02b-47ee-7913-b18b-d4d4b0be8b60","turn_id":"01a11557-fbc9-79d0-bdea-468251dfa6dd","session_id":"01a0a02b-47ee-7913-b18b-d4d4b0be8b60","root_turn_id":"01a11557-fbc9-79d0-bdea-468251dfa6dd","response_id":"resp_094cad5b47a7c03f016ac5fa2c33e487d2bd7b9931621b3da4","usage":{"input_tokens":97730,"cached_input_tokens":96000,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":286,"reasoning_output_tokens":133,"total_tokens":98016},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1365078,"cached_input_tokens":1266176,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":8489,"reasoning_output_tokens":2220,"total_tokens":1373567},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":150535332,"cached_input_tokens":146188160,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":611863,"reasoning_output_tokens":317563,"total_tokens":151147195}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T07:52:14.714Z","ordinal":10637,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0a02b-47ee-7913-b18b-d4d4b0be8b60","turn_id":"01a11557-fbc9-79d0-bdea-468251dfa6dd","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b1cbac22-efec-4944-9ed8-d574d47531d6","process_id":"54966","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","sed -n '120,155p' .ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md && sed -n '1,80p' docs/product-import-batch-resource.md && rg -n \"readme|xlsx|xlsx|openapi|API|failed|warning|successed|success\" docs/product-data-workflows.md docs/product-import-batch-resource.md docs/product-update-batch-resource.md docs/product-delete-batch-resource.md docs/shop-resource.md docs/configuration.md && git status --short"],"cwd":"file:///home/kamaz/www/strateg-projects/strateg-export-products","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '120,155p' .ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md && sed -n '1,80p' docs/product-import-batch-resource.md && rg -n \"readme|xlsx|xlsx|openapi|API|failed|warning|successed|success\" docs/product-data-workflows.md docs/product-import-batch-resource.md docs/product-update-batch-resource.md docs/product-delete-batch-resource.md docs/shop-resource.md docs/configuration.md && git status --short"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"### Export Module\n- Main code:\n  - `ProcessProductExportItemJob`\n  - `ProductPayloadBuilderService`\n  - `InteractsWithShopApi`\n- Responsibility:\n  - resolve shop-specific payload\n  - call remote API\n  - persist returned `external_product_id`\n\n### Remote API Boundary\n- Main code:\n  - `app-code/app/app/Jobs/Traits/InteractsWithShopApi.php`\n  - `app-code/app/app/Jobs/ProcessProductExportItemJob.php`\n  - `app-code/app/app/Jobs/ProcessProductUpdateItemJob.php`\n  - `app-code/app/app/Jobs/ProcessProductDeleteItemJob.php`\n  - `app-code/app/app/Jobs/ProcessCatalogProductRestoreItemJob.php`\n- Responsibility:\n  - resolve configurable remote endpoints and API base URLs\n  - authenticate OpenCart-like shops and refresh expired tokens\n  - send form-encoded export, update, backup, delete, and restore requests\n  - persist remote IDs and external backup snapshots\n- Boundary:\n  - this application has no inbound `routes/api.php`\n  - `docs/openapi.yaml` documents the outbound remote-shop integration as a configurable contract template\n  - the remote shop contract remains external and must be verified per integration\n  - endpoint configuration alone does not define every request or response field\n\n### Update / Delete / Restore Modules\n- Main code:\n  - `ProcessProductUpdateBatchJob`\n  - `ProductUpdateQueueService`\n  - `ProcessProductDeleteBatchJob`\n  - `ProductDeleteQueueService`\n  - `ProcessProductRestoreBatchJob`\n  - `ProcessCatalogProductRestoreBatchJob`\n[← Product Data Workflows](product-data-workflows.md) · [Back to README](../README.md) · [Product Updates →](product-update-batch-resource.md)\n\n# ProductImportBatchResource\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe ProductImports resource manages product imports from Excel, Google Sheets, or manual administration-panel input. It shows batch processing state and supports binding and exporting products to stores.\n\n## Resource Pages\n\n- index (ListProductImportBatches): import batch list.\n- create (CreateProductImportBatch): create an import batch.\n- view (ViewProductImportBatch): batch details and import items (ProductImportItemsRelationManager).\n\nTotal: 3 pages.\n\n## Input modes\n\nThe create form accepts an Excel file, a Google Sheets URL, or a manual admin form. Excel files must be `.xlsx` or `.xls` and contain the required worksheets and headers described in [Product Data Workflows](product-data-workflows.md). Google Sheets must expose the same worksheet structure to the configured Google service account.\n\n## How to Use\n\n1. Open Product Imports → Upload New Products.\n2. Select an Excel file, a Google Sheets URL, or Administration panel input.\n3. The batch is processed by ProcessProductImportBatchJob.\n4. Review statuses, payloads, product edits, store bindings, exports, and retries on the list or view page.\n\n## Statuses\n\nSource values: EXCEL, Google Sheets, and Administration panel.\n\nBatch statuses: New, Processing, Exporting to API, Completed, Failed, Partially failed, and Cancelled.\n\nImport item statuses: New, Processing, Normalized, Succeeded, and Failed.\n\nExport statuses: Not queued, Exporting, Exported, Export failed, and Partially failed.\n\n## Main Actions\n\n- View result.\n- Download or delete the error log.\n- Bulk-link products to stores.\n- Bulk-export products to stores.\n- Retry failed exports.\n- For an item: view payload, edit the product, export to stores, or retry failed exports.\n\nExport is shop-specific. A product must be bound to the selected shop before it can be exported. A successful remote response must provide an external product ID, which is saved for later updates, deletion, and restoration.\n\n## Common Validation Messages\n\n- Excel file is missing.\n- Google Sheets URL is invalid.\n- A required sheet or column is missing.\n- The Product sheet has no data.\n- The user is not authenticated.\n- The product is not linked to a store.\n\n## See Also\n\n- [Documentation Contents](README.md) — complete documentation index.\n- [Product Catalog](product-resource.md) — local product operations.\n- [Stores](shop-resource.md) — store integrations.\ndocs/configuration.md:11:Do not add passwords, API tokens, or other secrets to documentation or Git. Use container environment values for database access.\ndocs/configuration.md:22:| api_url                   | Custom API URL                                  |\ndocs/configuration.md:29:For OpenCart-like APIs, configure update, restore, deletion, and backup endpoints through options. The external product identifier is stored separately for each product-to-store relationship.\ndocs/configuration.md:37:Import, binding, export, update, deletion, and restoration run as queued jobs. Check batch and item statuses in the administration panel. External API errors are stored at operation level so the operation can be retried.\ndocs/product-import-batch-resource.md:19:The create form accepts an Excel file, a Google Sheets URL, or a manual admin form. Excel files must be `.xlsx` or `.xls` and contain the required worksheets and headers described in [Product Data Workflows](product-data-workflows.md). Google Sheets must expose the same worksheet structure to the configured Google service account.\ndocs/product-import-batch-resource.md:32:Batch statuses: New, Processing, Exporting to API, Completed, Failed, Partially failed, and Cancelled.\ndocs/product-import-batch-resource.md:36:Export statuses: Not queued, Exporting, Exported, Export failed, and Partially failed.\ndocs/product-import-batch-resource.md:44:- Retry failed exports.\ndocs/product-import-batch-resource.md:45:- For an item: view payload, edit the product, export to stores, or retry failed exports.\ndocs/product-import-batch-resource.md:47:Export is shop-specific. A product must be bound to the selected shop before it can be exported. A successful remote response must provide an external product ID, which is saved for later updates, deletion, and restoration.\ndocs/shop-resource.md:7:The resource manages online stores to which products, categories, and attributes are linked and where API requests are sent.\ndocs/shop-resource.md:23:- If api_url is empty, the API logic uses base_url.\ndocs/shop-resource.md:26:- The OpenAPI document describes outbound requests from this application; it is not an inbound API contract. See [Remote API Integration](remote-api-integration.md).\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:38:| Local Excel   | `.xlsx` or `.xls` upload                                                                                       | `ProcessProductImportBatchJob` | One normalized import item per product row                                                                  |\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:55:- the export item is not already processing or successfully exported.\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:57:`ProductPayloadBuilderService` builds a shop-scoped payload containing the product, descriptions, images, categories, attributes, manufacturer, brand, specials, discounts, and active shop languages. A successful remote response must contain an external product ID. That ID is saved to `spme_product_shop.external_product_id` and is required for later update, delete, and restore operations.\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:71:The API update job creates an external backup before the remote update, builds a shop-scoped payload, and calls the configured update endpoint. Products without a shop binding or external ID are skipped and reported in the action summary.\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:73:The catalog edit page uses the same update queue service for field-level API modes. Each field can be skipped, deleted, or updated, and the resulting instructions are stored with the update item.\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:77:Product Deletes accepts Excel or Google Sheets documents. The `Product` sheet resolves a target by `Product Id`, or by a combination of `Shop Id` and one or more of `External Product Id`, `Model`, or `EAN`. A row with no identifier becomes a failed delete item instead of being silently ignored.\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:96:| Import/update/delete batch | `new`, `processing`, `completed`, `failed`, `partial_failed`, `canceled` | Batch table       |\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:97:| Import/update item         | `new`, `processing`, `normalized`, `successed`, `failed`, `not_queued`   | Item table        |\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:98:| Delete item                | `new`, `processing`, `deleted`, `failed`                                 | Delete item table |\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:99:| Export item                | `processing`, `normalized`, `exported`, `partial_failed`, `failed`       | Export item table |\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:101:Use the batch counters and item records as the operational source of truth. Check `options.last_error`, `options.error_log_path`, and the linked error-log snapshot when a batch is partially or fully failed.\ndocs/product-data-workflows.md:107:- [Remote API Integration](remote-api-integration.md) — outbound shop requests and API status.\ndocs/product-delete-batch-resource.md:20:When several lookup values are supplied, they are intersected and must resolve to one product. An ambiguous or unresolved row becomes a failed delete item with its source row and error message retained.\ndocs/product-delete-batch-resource.md:30:Deletion requires a `spme_product_shop` binding and a non-empty `external_product_id`. The remote backup is stored in `spme_product_backups` before deletion when the shop API supports the configured backup endpoint.\ndocs/product-delete-batch-resource.md:34:Batch statuses are `new`, `processing`, `completed`, `failed`, `partial_failed`, and `canceled`. Item statuses are `new`, `processing`, `deleted`, and `failed`.\ndocs/product-delete-batch-resource.md:39:- [Remote API Integration](remote-api-integration.md) — delete, backup, and restore request configuration.\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:7:The ProductUpdates resource uploads update batches and performs bulk or individual product updates in stores through their APIs.\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:22:4. Inspect items and payloads, update stores in bulk or individually, and retry failed updates.\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:24:The `Product` sheet identifies a product with `Product Id`, or with `Shop Id` plus one or more of `External Product Id`, `Model`, and `EAN`. When several identifiers are supplied, they must resolve to the same product. The preparation job creates a local backup, applies local changes, and stores the remote update instructions in the item payload before an API update is queued.\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:28:Sources: CSV file, Excel file, Google Sheet, Local products, and Individual API update from Edit Product.\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:30:Batch statuses: New, Processing, Updating through API, Completed, Failed, Partially failed, and Cancelled.\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:37:- Retry failed updates.\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:38:- For an item: view payload, update stores, or retry failed updates.\ndocs/product-update-batch-resource.md:44:- The record is already queued, updated, or already has a failed record.\n M README.md\n M docs/README.md\n M docs/agent-collaboration.md\n M docs/architecture.md\n M docs/category-resource.md\n M docs/getting-started.md\n M docs/opencart-api-token-lifecycle.md\n M docs/remote-api-integration.md\n M docs/shop-resource.md\n M docs/user-resource.md\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"### Export Module\n- Main code:\n  - `ProcessProductExportItemJob`\n  - `ProductPayloadBuilderService`\n  - `InteractsWithShopApi`\n- Responsibility:\n  - resolve shop-specific payload\n  - call remote API\n  - persist returned `external_product_id`\n\n### Remote API Boundary\n- Main code:\n  - `app-code/app/app/Jobs/Traits/InteractsWithShopApi.php`\n  - `app-code/app/app/Jobs/ProcessProductExportItemJob.php`\n  - `app-code/app/app/Jobs/ProcessProductUpdateItemJob.php`\n  - `app-code/app/app/Jobs/ProcessProductDeleteItemJob.php`\n  - `app-code/app/app/Jobs/ProcessCatalogProductRestoreItemJob.php`\n- Responsibility:\n  - resolve configurable remote endpoints and API base URLs\n  - authenticate OpenCart-like shops and refresh expired tokens\n  - send form-encoded export, update, backup, delete, and restore requests\n  - persist remote IDs and external backup snapshots\n- Boundary:\n  - this application has no inbound `routes/api.php`\n  - `docs/openapi.yaml` documents the outbound remote-shop integration as a configurable contract template\n  - the remote shop contract remains external and must be verified per integration\n  - endpoint configuration alone does not define every request or response field\n\n### Update / Delete / Restore Modules\n- Main code:\n  - `ProcessProductUpdateBatchJob`\n  - `ProductUpdateQueueService`\n  - `ProcessProductDeleteBatchJob`\n  - `ProductDeleteQueueService`\n  - `ProcessProductRestoreBatchJob`\n  - `ProcessCatalogProductRestoreBatchJob`\n[← Product Data Workflows](product-data-workflows.md) · [Back to README](../README.md) · [Product Updates →](product-update-batch-resource.md)\n\n# ProductImportBatchResource\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe ProductImports resource manages product imports from Excel, Google Sheets, or manual administration-panel input. It shows batch processing state and supports binding and exporting products to stores.\n\n## Resource Pages\n\n- index (ListProductImportBatches): import batch list.\n- create (CreateProductImportBatch): create an import batch.\n- view (ViewProductImportBatch): batch details and import items (ProductImportItemsRelationManager).\n\nTotal: 3 pages.\n\n## Input modes\n\nThe create form accepts an Excel file, a Google Sheets URL, or a manual admin form. Excel files must be `.xlsx` or `.xls` and contain the required worksheets and headers described in [Product Data Workflows](product-data-workflows.md). Google Sheets must expose the same worksheet structure to the configured Google service account.\n\n## How to Use\n\n1. Open Product Imports → Upload New Products.\n2. Select an Excel file, a Google Sheets URL, or Administration panel input.\n3. The batch is processed by ProcessProductImportBatchJob.\n4. Review statuses, payloads, product edits, store bindings, exports, and retries on the list or view page.\n\n## Statuses\n\nSource values: EXCEL, Google Sheets, and Administration panel.\n\nBatch statuses: New, Processing, Exporting to API, Completed, Failed, Partially failed, and Cancelled.\n\nImport item statuses: New, Processing, Normalized, Succeeded, and Failed.\n\nExport statuses: Not queued, Exporting, Exported, Export f