; host parsers and language tools are separate. From the `ai-code-intelligence` repository root, inspect service and database docs, then connect using the documented command:\n.codex/skills/ai-use-knowledge/references/RETRIEVAL-PLAYBOOK.md:34:  ai-code-intelligence-postgres-postgresql sh -lc \\\n.codex/skills/ai-use-knowledge/SKILL.md:3:description: Searches project code and documentation with local tools and the shared ai-code-intelligence index, including PostgreSQL full-text/vector search, Serena, ast-grep, Tree-sitter, and ripgrep. Use when locating implementations, tracing behavior, or building evidence-backed explanations from indexed code.\n.codex/skills/ai-use-knowledge/SKILL.md:17:Start with this repository's `AGENTS.md` and follow its links to the shared project. In `/home/kamaz/www/hobby/ai-code-intelligence/`, read `AGENTS.md` and `README.md`, then consult the relevant pages:\n.codex/skills/ai-use-knowledge/SKILL.md:19:- [Agent workflow](../../../../../hobby/ai-code-intelligence/docs/agent-workflow.md)\n.codex/skills/ai-use-knowledge/SKILL.md:20:- [Retrieval and indexing](../../../../../hobby/ai-code-intelligence/docs/retrieval-and-indexing.md)\n.codex/skills/ai-use-knowledge/SKILL.md:21:- [Architecture and tool responsibilities](../../../../../hobby/ai-code-intelligence/docs/architecture.md)\n.codex/skills/ai-use-knowledge/SKILL.md:22:- [Database schema and ownership](../../../../../hobby/ai-code-intelligence/docs/database.md)\n.codex/skills/ai-use-knowledge/SKILL.md:23:- [Security guidance](../../../../../hobby/ai-code-intelligence/docs/security.md)\n.codex/skills/ai-use-knowledge/SKILL.md:24:- [Tool integrations](../../../../../hobby/ai-code-intelligence/docs/integrations.md)\n.codex/skills/ai-use-knowledge/SKILL.md:34:5. Use the project-scoped PostgreSQL index when wording is unknown, code is spread across files, or local search has not exposed the relevant concepts.\n.codex/skills/ai-use-knowledge/SKILL.md:45:- Use the database through the documented Docker service; do not assume PostgreSQL or parsers are installed in the same environment.\n.codex/skills/laravel-fullstack-admin-suite/SKILL.md:26:- Project-aligned fullstack work for Laravel 13 + Filament 5 + Livewire 4.\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/PROJECT-DOCUMENTATION.md:1:# Project Documentation and `ai-code-intelligence.md`\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/PROJECT-DOCUMENTATION.md:12:6. If the project shares the AI Code Intelligence database, add `docs/ai-code-intelligence.md`. Include it in the README Documentation table and `AGENTS.md` Documentation table.\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/PROJECT-DOCUMENTATION.md:15:## Creating `docs/ai-code-intelligence.md`\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/PROJECT-DOCUMENTATION.md:57:- When commands or DB behavior change, update the relevant shared AI Code Intelligence docs and the project `ai-code-intelligence.md` only when the user/task includes that scope.\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/AI-CODE-INTELLIGENCE.md:7:/home/kamaz/www/hobby/ai-code-intelligence/\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/AI-CODE-INTELLIGENCE.md:42:ast-grep run --lang php --pattern 'class $NAME extends $BASE' httpdocs\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/AI-CODE-INTELLIGENCE.md:47:For Serena, inspect the installed CLI first (`serena --help`). Run project indexing from the repository root using the command exposed by that version (in this setup, `serena project index`). A PHP language server may be downloaded on first run; DNS failure to a package registry does not mean the source project is invalid. Retry only after network availability is restored.\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/AI-CODE-INTELLIGENCE.md:51:The local service is named `ai-code-intelligence-postgres-postgresql`. It provides PostgreSQL and Node.js. Use the Compose file at:\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/AI-CODE-INTELLIGENCE.md:54:/home/kamaz/www/hobby/ai-code-intelligence/.docker/dev/docker-compose.yml\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/AI-CODE-INTELLIGENCE.md:70:/home/kamaz/www/hobby/ai-code-intelligence/app/embedding-results/\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/AI-CODE-INTELLIGENCE.md:73:The same directory is visible in the container as `/app/embedding-results/`. Use deterministic batch filenames and a manifest containing each batch filename, chunk IDs, content hashes, model, and dimensions. Persist every successful batch before moving to the next one.\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/AI-CODE-INTELLIGENCE.md:80:docker compose -f /home/kamaz/www/hobby/ai-code-intelligence/.docker/dev/docker-compose.yml \\\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/AI-CODE-INTELLIGENCE.md:81:  exec -T ai-code-intelligence-postgres-postgresql sh -lc '\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/references/AI-CODE-INTELLIGENCE.md:83:      /app/embedding-results/project-batch-0000.json \\\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/SKILL.md:2:name: ai-code-intelligence\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/SKILL.md:3:description: Explains how to use the shared ai-code-intelligence documentation, host-side code tools, PostgreSQL retrieval, and paid embeddings safely. Use when indexing or searching a project in the shared intelligence database, or when creating/updating project documentation about that integration, especially docs/ai-code-intelligence.md.\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/SKILL.md:13:Use this skill to work with the shared `ai-code-intelligence` project and document that workflow accurately. Treat the repository as an evidence store, not as an authority over the source code.\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/SKILL.md:17:1. Identify the current repository root and read its `AGENTS.md` first. Follow direct links to the shared `ai-code-intelligence` project; do not guess its path.\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/SKILL.md:29:For tool commands, index recovery, vector search, and common failures, read [the detailed workflow reference](references/AI-CODE-INTELLIGENCE.md).\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/SKILL.md:39:- Unknown business wording: PostgreSQL full-text and vector retrieval.\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/SKILL.md:42:Check which environment has the tools. In this setup, PostgreSQL and Node.js run in Docker; `ast-grep`, Tree-sitter Python bindings, and Serena are host tools. A missing command inside the database container does not establish that it is absent on the host. Check `command -v`, `serena --version`, and the Python interpreter that can import `tree_sitter_language_pack`.\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/SKILL.md:53:4. Write each batch immediately to the configured persistent `app/embedding-results/` directory. Never keep the only copy in container `/tmp`.\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/SKILL.md:56:The current `app/embedding.js` prints its API key and input texts to stdout. Suppress that output and do not expose captured logs. In the local Compose setup, the host results directory is mounted at `/app/embedding-results/` inside the PostgreSQL/Node container. See [the paid-embedding and recovery instructions](references/AI-CODE-INTELLIGENCE.md#paid-embeddings-and-safe-retries).\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/SKILL.md:62:3. Generate and persist embedding batch files, then write vectors to PostgreSQL.\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/SKILL.md:73:When a project uses the shared intelligence database, create a `docs/ai-code-intelligence.md` page. Document:\n.codex/skills/ai-code-intelligence/SKILL.md:85:Use [the documentation checklist and page outline](references/PROJECT-DOCUMENTATION.md) for first-time documentation and `docs/ai-code-intelligence.md` updates.\n.codex/skills/php-best-practices/SKILL.md:59:- Align with project stack conventions: Laravel 13, Filament 5, Livewire 4.\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/references/BEST-PRACTICES.md:208:# PostgreSQL\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/references/BEST-PRACTICES.md:317:  - postgres_data:/var/lib/postgresql/data\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/references/BEST-PRACTICES.md:519:| PostgreSQL | 2.0 | 1G | 256M |\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/references/BEST-PRACTICES.md:533:| PostgreSQL | 5432 | — |\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/references/SECURITY-CHECKLIST.md:56:| PostgreSQL | `DAC_READ_SEARCH`, `FOWNER`, `SETGID`, `SETUID` |\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/references/SECURITY-CHECKLIST.md:85:| PostgreSQL | `5432:5432` | None |\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/references/SECURITY-CHECKLIST.md:112:  - PostgreSQL: `pg_isready -U $USER -d $DB`\n.codex/skills/aif-ci/references/SERVICE-CONTAINERS.md:36:    DATABASE_URL: \"REDACTED\"\n.codex/skills/aif-distillation/references/LARGE-MATERIALS.md:10:python3 --version\n.codex/skills/aif-distillation/references/LARGE-MATERIALS.md:18:- `python3 --version` -> `python3`\n.codex/skills/aif-distillation/references/LARGE-MATERIALS.md:26:python3 .codex/skills/aif-distillation/scripts/material-prep.py <source...>\n.codex/skills/aif-distillation/references/LARGE-MATERIALS.md:79:python3 .codex/skills/aif-distillation/scripts/material-prep.py --cleanup <temp-dir>\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/SKILL.md:106:1. PostgreSQL (Recommended)\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/SKILL.md:107:2. MySQL / MariaDB\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/SKILL.md:223:Grep: postgres|postgresql|pg_|mysql|mariadb|mongo|mongodb|sqlite\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/SKILL.md:249:- Specific variant (MySQL vs PostgreSQL, Redis vs Memcached)\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/SKILL.md:371:For infrastructure images (PostgreSQL, Redis, Angie, Nginx, etc.) — the version is NOT in project files. Before generating compose.yml, use `WebSearch` to check the current stable version of each infrastructure image:\n.codex/skills/aif-dockerize/SKILL.md:385:  - PostgreSQL / MySQL / MongoDB → with healthcheck, named volume\n.codex/skills/livewire-development/SKILL.md:3:description: \"Use for any task or question involving Livewire. Activate if user mentions Livewire, wire: directives, or Livewire-specific concepts like wire:model, wire:click, wire:sort, or islands, invoke this skill. Covers building new components, debugging reactivity issues, real-time form validation, drag-and-drop, loading states, migrating from Livewire 3 to 4, converting component formats (SFC/MFC/class-based), and performance optimization. Do not use for non-Livewire reactive UI (React, Vue, Alpine-only, Inertia.js) or standard Laravel forms without Livewire.\"\n.codex/skills/livewire-development/SKILL.md:100:### Key Changes From Livewire 3\n.codex/skills/aif/SKILL.md:5:allowed-tools: Read Glob Grep Write Bash(mkdir *) Bash(node *update-config.mjs*) Bash(npx skills *) Bash(python3 --version) Bash(python --version) Bash(py -3 --version) Bash(py --version) Bash(python3 *security-scan.py*) Bash(python *security-scan.py*) Bash(py -3 *security-scan.py*) Bash(py *security-scan.py*) Bash(python3 *cleanup-blocked-skill.py*) Bash(python *cleanup-blocked-skill.py*) Bash(py -3 *cleanup-blocked-skill.py*) Bash(py *cleanup-blocked-skill.py*) Skill WebFetch AskUserQuestion Questions\n.codex/skills/aif/SKILL.md:26:python3 --version\n.codex/skills/aif/SKILL.md:33:  - `python3 --version` → `PYTHON_CMD=(python3)`\n.codex/skills/aif/SKILL.md:40:  1. Provide path to Python (e.g., `/usr/local/bin/python3.11`)\n.codex/skills/aif/SKILL.md:58:# Example for PYTHON_CMD=(python3); use python, py -3, or py only if that was the selected Python 3 command.\n.codex/skills/aif/SKILL.md:59:python3 ~/.codex/skills/aif-skill-generator/scripts/security-scan.py <installed-skill-path>\n.codex/skills/aif/SKILL.md:61:- When calling Bash, expand `PYTHON_CMD` to the selected command shape, for example `python3 ...security-scan.py` or `py -3 ...security-scan.py`; do not run arbitrary Python payloads.\n.codex/skills/aif/SKILL.md:63:- **Exit 1 (BLOCKED)** → Remove via cleanup helper using the same selected Python 3 command, for example `python3 ~/.codex/skills/aif-skill-generator/scripts/cleanup-blocked-skill.py --skill <skill-name> --installed-path <installed-skill-path>`. Pass the **same `<installed-skill-path>` you just scanned** — do not synthesize the path from `<skill-name>` (upstream `skills` CLI sanitizes the directory name, so a logical name like `\"Convex Best Practices\"` lives on disk as `convex-best-practices`). The helper deletes the skill directory AND clears its entry from `skills-lock.json` so the blocked skill cannot be resurrected; `--installed-path` lets it verify physical removal and return an exact exit code. Warn user with full threat details. **NEVER use.**\n.codex/skills/aif/SKILL.md:347:| Prisma/PostgreSQL | `db-migrations` | `postgres` |\n.codex/skills/aif/SKILL.md:395:   # AUTO-SCAN: immediately after install. Example for PYTHON_CMD=(python3).\n.codex/skills/aif/SKILL.md:396:   python3 ~/.codex/skills/aif-skill-generator/scripts/security-scan.py <installed-path>\n.codex/skills/aif/SKILL.md:556:**When:** Uses PostgreSQL, Prisma, Drizzle, Supabase\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/SKILL.md:3:description: Indexes project code and documentation into the shared ai-code-intelligence database, creates evidence-backed knowledge and paid embeddings, and performs safe project-scoped CRUD. Use when creating or refreshing an index, managing knowledge items, generating embeddings, or reading/writing AI Code Intelligence PostgreSQL data.\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/SKILL.md:13:Use this skill for operational work in the shared `ai-code-intelligence` repository and PostgreSQL database. Before relying on a command or schema detail, read the shared repository's `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, and relevant docs, then confirm table/function names in the checked-in SQL.\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/SKILL.md:18:2. Check the host tools and Docker service separately. In this setup PostgreSQL and Node.js are in Docker; Serena, ast-grep, and Tree-sitter Python bindings are host tools.\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/references/INDEXING-WORKFLOW.md:3:The shared repository is `/home/kamaz/www/hobby/ai-code-intelligence/`. Start with its `AGENTS.md` and `README.md`, then read `docs/getting-started.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/database.md`, `docs/retrieval-and-indexing.md`, `docs/agent-workflow.md`, and `docs/security.md` as relevant. The DDL in `docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/` is authoritative.\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/references/INDEXING-WORKFLOW.md:7:Check tools on the host. The local PostgreSQL/Node container does not need to contain parsers or language servers.\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/references/INDEXING-WORKFLOW.md:16:Use the Python interpreter that can import `tree_sitter_language_pack`; verify rather than assuming `python3` points to it. Serena can install a PHP language server during initial indexing. If DNS/package registry access fails, treat it as a tool setup issue and retry when available.\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/references/INDEXING-WORKFLOW.md:21:ast-grep run --lang php --pattern 'class $NAME extends $BASE' httpdocs\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/references/INDEXING-WORKFLOW.md:23:serena project index\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/references/INDEXING-WORKFLOW.md:28:## Connect to PostgreSQL Through Docker\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/references/INDEXING-WORKFLOW.md:34:  ai-code-intelligence-postgres-postgresql sh -lc \\\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/references/INDEXING-WORKFLOW.md:70:/home/kamaz/www/hobby/ai-code-intelligence/app/embedding-results/\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/references/INDEXING-WORKFLOW.md:73:Container output path: `/app/embedding-results/`. Use stable per-batch filenames. Before calling the API, compare files and chunk hashes so completed inputs are not charged twice. Keep a manifest mapping each output file to project ID, model ID, chunk IDs, content hashes, and dimensions.\n.codex/skills/ai-create-knowledge/references/INDEXING-WORKFLOW.md:78:docker compose -f /home/kamaz/www/hobby/ai-code-intelligence/.docker/dev/docker-compose.yml \\\n.codex/s